---
import DownloadButtons from "../../download/DownloadButtons.astro";
import GuidePage from "../../guide/GuidePage.astro";
import Question from "../../guide/Question.astro";
import { leavesSite, RELEASES, sitePath } from "../../site/links.ts";
---

<GuidePage slug="install" lead="Which file to get, how updates work, and how to bring your library over from Mihon.">
  <Question id="which-file" question="Which file should I download?" open>
    <p>
      Katari runs on phones and tablets with Android 10 or newer. Most people want <strong>Katari</strong>. The
      same app without Google services is <strong>Katari FOSS</strong>, which never sends crash logs or usage data.
    </p>
    <DownloadButtons explained={false} />
    <p>
      The <a href={`${RELEASES}/latest`} {...leavesSite()}>release page</a> also has smaller files made for one type of
      processor. Most phones from recent years take arm64-v8a, and older ones take armeabi-v7a. If you're not sure, the
      buttons above work on every phone.
    </p>
  </Question>

  <Question id="updates" question="Does Katari update itself?">
    <p>
      Yes, both builds do. When a new version is out, Katari offers to download and install it. Android asks once
      for permission to let Katari install apps.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you use the mpv add-on and the new version needs a newer one, the update brings it along and installs it first, so mpv keeps
      working.
    </p>
  </Question>

  <Question id="mpv-addon" question="What is the mpv add-on?">
    <p>
      An optional second app that lets Katari play videos in mpv, for formats and styled subtitles the built-in player can't handle.
      Install it from Katari under Settings › Players › Anime player, or when a video asks for it.
      <a href={sitePath("guide/video/#mpv-addon")}>Watching video</a> explains how it updates and how to remove it.
    </p>
  </Question>

  <Question id="from-mihon" question="Can I bring my library over from Mihon?">
    <p>
      Yes. In Mihon, create a backup containing everything you want to keep, then choose it when Katari's setup
      offers <em>Move from Mihon</em>. Tick <em>Include sensitive settings</em> to bring source preferences and sign-ins along.
      <a href={sitePath("guide/backups-and-storage/#mihon")}>Backups and storage</a> walks through it.
    </p>
    <p>
      To keep your downloads, select the storage folder Mihon used. Extensions installed privately in Mihon have to be
      installed again in Katari, and ones made for an old extension library need their current version.
    </p>
  </Question>

  <Question id="content" question="Where does the content come from?">
    <p>
      Katari comes with no content and has no affiliation with any provider. Content comes from extensions you
      choose. Add an extension store under Browse › Extensions, then install the extensions you want from it.
      <a href={sitePath("guide/first-steps/")}>First steps</a> walks through it.
    </p>
  </Question>

  <Question id="data-sent" question="What does Katari send, and can I turn it off?">
    <p>
      Katari can send anonymized crash logs and usage data. Its setup shows both as switches, and you can change
      them any time in Settings › Security and privacy. Katari FOSS sends neither.
    </p>
  </Question>
</GuidePage>
